# p5 mcp: a stdio server that exits 3 at start (p5-mcp-fail's profile), its
# screen opened between two of its tries. The tries come at a 1 s backoff
# that doubles (xfx src/mcp/runtime.rs:90), near 1, 3, 7, 15 and 31 s after
# launch; the screen is opened near 9 s, two seconds after one and six before
# the next, and snapped a second later. xfx answers the screen's tools request
# from the last try's failure (src/tui/mcp_menu.rs:786-791): `Its tools
# couldn't load`. fx shows `Loading tools…` until its next try, near 15 s
# (receipts/launch-settle). LAUNCH-SETTLE added this scenario to keep that
# difference on a snap, since p5-mcp-fail now waits it out.
fx: homefile .fx/mcp.json p5-mcp-fail-profile.json
xfx: homefile .xfx/mcp.json p5-mcp-fail-profile.json
wait 9
type /mcp
key Enter
until shown MCP servers  2
key Enter
until shown echo boom-stderr >&2; exit 3
wait 1
snap held
key Escape
wait 0.5
key Escape
